THOUGHT: Now I understand the issue. When the backtrace frame has `args`, the serializer is called on those args. If one of the args is a string that happens to be a class name (like `Vendor\Customer\Plugin\Api\CustomerRepositoryPlugin`), then `is_callable($value)` will trigger the autoloader to load that class. If the class file has a problem (like a redeclare issue), this triggers an exception during serialization.

